# Project conventions

These apply to every change in this repository. Check them again before each push.

## Licences

Third-party libraries, tools, and runtime dependencies must be MIT or Apache-2.0 only. If a needed library is not MIT or Apache-2.0, pick an MIT or Apache-2.0 alternative or ask.

## Git identity

Pushes go out only as nordlyse. Author and committer must be Jakob Lyse <jakob.lyse@gmail.com>.

Before every push, check the commits that would be sent:

- `git log` author and committer are Jakob Lyse <jakob.lyse@gmail.com>
- No `Co-authored-by` trailer for Cursor, cursoragent, or any other agent
- No other GitHub identity in author, committer, or trailers

If another identity is present, strip it before the push. Do not push until the check passes.

## Language

Comments, class names, `README.md`, docs, and other written text are English.

## Wording

Do not use the word "create" in method names, class names, comments, `README.md`, docs, or commit messages. Use "add" or "insert" instead.

```java
// Avoid: createUser, UserCreator
// Use: addUser, insertUser
```

A framework API that requires that word may stay, for example `document.createElement` or `Files.createDirectories`.
